<p>The server code is rather straightforward:</p>
<ul>
<li class="">As usual we start by establishing the connection and declaring
the queue <code>rpc_queue</code>.</li>
<li class="">We declare our fibonacci function. It assumes only valid positive integer input.
(Don't expect this one to work for big numbers,
it's probably the slowest recursive implementation possible).</li>
<li class="">We consume messages from the queue, and for each request
we do the work and send the response back.</li>
<li class="">We might want to run more than one server process. In order
to spread the load equally over multiple servers we need to set the
<code>prefetchCount</code> setting via <code>basicQos</code>.</li>
</ul>
